{"title":"Legendre Conjecture","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The Legendre Conjecture is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Conjecture\" title=\"Conjecture\">conjecture</a> in number theory. It had been presented more than a century ago yet still unsolved. It is one of the famous <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Landau%27s_Problems\" title=\"Landau&#39;s Problems\">Landau's Problems</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Statement\">Statement</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Legendre_Conjecture&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Statement\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The conjecture states that there is a prime between every two pairs of consecutive squares of integers. I.e., for each integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> there exist a prime number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> such that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/5/9d5ef2039fb8ba223585b1d8a25d5f1e0f9f0f06.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^2 &lt; p &lt; (n+1)^2\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Legendre_Conjecture&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018093143\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.008 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.013 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 20/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 516/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.412      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.412      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:30399:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018093143 and revision id 238698. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}